 @ImJustACowLol  Youtube supports h265 for uploads but re-encodes the data to a different codec. Youtube and Twitch do not support h265 streaming as well as h265 comes with heaps of royalties that can be averted by using open source codecs like vp9 and av01. H264 on the other hand is super lightweight and easy to process. I am pretty sure it has royalties but the processing power it takes to run is very tiny in comparison to h265 making it FAR more useful for reducing bandwidth.
If you dont believe me ask why youtube is lowering default quality and testing different lower resolutions. Why do they hide av01 preference defaulted to off? Why do they want to charge for 4k content? Because most users dont care, if it is good enough to watch it is good enough for them.
I love using h265 when i record for the qualty boost, but there is no way I am using it once i get a card capable of av01 encoding, not a single chance.
